ACT ONE

SCENE ONE

A bare stage. A single chair sits center, lit by a narrow spotlight.

MARGARET enters slowly, carrying a worn leather suitcase.

MARGARET
I told myself I wouldn't come back here.

She sets the suitcase down and regards the empty chair.

MARGARET
And yet.

THOMAS
(from offstage)
Maggie? Is that you?

MARGARET
(startled)
Tom. I didn't think you still lived here.

THOMAS enters from stage left, older than we expect, gentler too.

THOMAS
Where else would I go?

They stand in silence. The spotlight widens to include them both.

BLACKOUT

END OF ACT
